  "caption": "Quinn discovered leg day, went for the deepest squats in the gym, and got a pinch at the front of the hip. Then came the googling, and the panic.\n\nHip pinch in young gym-goers is often a mix of hip shape and load, not damage. Plenty of people with this hip shape have no pain at all, and it usually responds to rehab.\n\nWhat often helps: adjust squat depth, stance and long sitting for now, strengthen your glutes, deep hip and trunk, bring depth back in stages, and track your training load. Expect three months or more.\n\nIf catching or locking persists after proper rehab, a further review is worth it.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
